WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为您制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉您的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.550
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:25.390
All right, everybody.
好了，各位。

9
00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.390
We are still saying goodbye to Toby.
我们还在向托比告别。

10
00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.470
It is Goodbye, Toby, Part 2.
这是《再见，托比》的第二部分。

11
00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.430
It's a long goodbye, but he deserves it.
这是一个漫长的告别，但他值得。

12
00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.030
He's been at the company a long time.
他在公司待了很久。

13
00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:36.330
He deserves a two-parter.
他值得拥有两集告别篇。

14
00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.850
Michael's going to give him a big send-off, lady.
迈克尔要为他举办一场盛大的欢送会，女士。

15
00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.050
He sure is.
他确实会。

16
00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:48.410
Guys, it's Season 4, Episode 19, written by Jen Salata and Paul Lieberstein, directed by Paul Feig.
伙计们，这是第四季第十九集，由简·萨拉塔和保罗·利伯斯坦编剧，保罗·费格执导。

17
00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:52.310
Here is a summary of Part 2 of Goodbye, Toby.
以下是《再见，托比》第二部分的剧情摘要。

18
00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:53.090
Okay.
好的。

19
00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:59.850
An extravagant goodbye party is being thrown in the parking lot for Toby.
停车场正在为托比举办一场奢华的告别派对。

20
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.730
Ryan is arrested for fraud.
瑞安因欺诈被捕。

21
00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:05.770
Michael discovers big news about Jan.
迈克尔发现了关于简的重大新闻。

22
00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:10.810
Jim plans to propose to Pam, but gets upstaged by Andy.
吉姆计划向帕姆求婚，却被安迪抢了风头。

23
00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.410
And Phyllis discovers a secret.
菲利斯发现了一个秘密。

24
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.190
Does she ever?
她确实发现了，不是吗？

25
00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:18.770
All right.
好吧。

26
00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:19.950
Jumping right in.
直接进入正题。

27
00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:21.410
Fast fact number one.
第一个速览事实。

28
00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:23.590
I'm calling this Party Time.
我把它称为“派对时间”。

29
00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:26.490
Are you going to give me a breakdown of all the party?
你要给我详细介绍一下整个派对吗？

30
00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.050
You know I am.
你知道我会的。

31
00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:32.570
We got fan questions from Abby M and Yvette M.
我们收到了来自艾比·M和伊薇特·M的粉丝提问。

32
00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:36.770
How many days did it take to film Toby's goodbye party?
拍摄托比的告别派对花了几天时间？

33
00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.210
How long did it take to set it up?
布置现场花了多久？

34
00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.450
Well, you know I went to Kentopedia.
嗯，你知道我查了“肯特百科”。

35
00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:48.050
He said it took one full day to set it up and two days and nights to film.
他说布置现场花了一整天，拍摄则用了两个昼夜。

36
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:53.310
We filmed April 17th and 18th of 2008.
我们是在2008年4月17日和18日拍摄的。

37
00:01:53.970 --> 00:02:02.390
The Ferris wheel came from a company called Awesome Events, and it cost us $7,500 to rent
摩天轮来自一家叫“超棒活动”的公司，租用那个摩天轮三天花了我们7500美元。

38
00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:04.170
that Ferris wheel for three days.
租用那个摩天轮三天。

39
00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:05.310
Dang.
天哪。

40
00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:06.190
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

41
00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:08.530
That's a pricey Ferris wheel.
那可真是个昂贵的摩天轮。

42
00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.510
Here's what I remember about those party scenes, Angela.
安吉拉，关于那些派对场景，我记得这些。

43
00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:14.410
It was very hot during the day.
白天非常热。

44
00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.210
And then at night, it got cold.
然后到了晚上，又变冷了。

45
00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:16.850
Yeah.
是啊。

46
00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:20.270
I remember I had hand warmers in my pockets at night.
我记得晚上我口袋里放着暖手宝。

47
00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:25.230
And you know when you go skiing and you put those toe warmers in your ski boots?
你知道滑雪时会把那种暖脚贴放进滑雪靴里吗？

48
00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:28.310
I had those in my shoes for the night shoot.
夜间拍摄时，我把那种暖脚贴放进了鞋子里。

49
00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:32.290
Also, whenever they didn't see our feet, we had Uggs on.
而且，只要镜头拍不到我们的脚，我们就穿着雪地靴。

50
00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:36.470
And Jenna, I have an Ugg catch later in this episode.
珍娜，这一集后面我有一个关于雪地靴的发现。

51
00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.270
Whose Uggs do you see?
你看到谁的雪地靴了？

52
00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:39.550
Not going to tell.
我不告诉你。

53
00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:43.890
Guys, you're going to have to wait for it.
伙计们，你们得等一等。

54
00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:45.990
She's making you wait for it.
她在吊你们胃口呢。

55
00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:52.650
But also, in between takes, do you remember our wardrobe department had these big, puffy
而且，在拍摄间隙，你们还记得我们的服装部门有那种大大的、蓬松的

56
00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:57.150
coats, like the kind that go down to your ankles, giant puffy coats, and they would bring
外套吗？就是那种长到脚踝的，巨大的羽绒服，他们会拿

57
00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:02.850
them out to us so that we could put them on in between takes outside when we were cold.
给我们穿，这样我们在户外拍摄感到冷的时候，可以在间隙穿上。

58
00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:04.190
And you know what?
你们知道吗？

59
00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:05.010
What?
什么？

60
00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:06.670
I still have mine.
我还留着我的那件。

61
00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:07.770
You do?
真的吗？

62
00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:09.330
Oh, what a score.
噢，真是赚到了。

63
00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:10.050
Yeah.
是啊。

64
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:15.850
And on the label, on the inside of the coat, it says Pam, written in Sharpie.
在衣服内侧的标签上，用记号笔写着“Pam”。

65
00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:16.890
Aww.
噢。

66
00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:19.770
Because that's how they knew whose coat belonged to who.
因为那是他们区分谁是谁的外套的方法。

67
00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:20.590
They Sharpied it.
他们用记号笔写上去的。

68
00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:22.930
Well, these were like giant sleeping bags.
那简直就像巨大的睡袋。

69
00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:23.470
Yes.
没错。

70
00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:24.650
Made into jackets.
做成了夹克的样子。

71
00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.270
Well described.
形容得很贴切。

72
00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.130
Okay, fast fact number two.
好了，第二个小知识点。

73
00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:30.930
I'm kind of sad.
我有点难过。

74
00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:32.470
I know.
我知道。

75
00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.690
This is not just goodbye, Toby.
这不仅仅是告别托比。

76
00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:35.670
Nope.
没错。

77
00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.910
This is goodbye, Kentopedia.
这是在告别“肯特百科”。

78
00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:39.070
Yes.
是的。

79
00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:40.450
Kent Svornak.
肯特·斯沃纳克。

80
00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.790
This was the end of his run on the office.
这是他在《办公室》工作的终点。

81
00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:43.570
Yeah.
是啊。

82
00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.810
After this, he moved on.
在那之后，他继续前行。

83
00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:53.730
And he became the producer and production manager for Anger Management, Dear White People,
他成为了《愤怒管理》、《亲爱的白人》的制片人和制作经理，

84
00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:56.230
and most recently, The Conners.
最近还参与了《康纳一家》。

85
00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:00.910
He is an amazing, amazing production manager, you guys.
他是一位非常、非常出色的制作经理，伙计们。

86
00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:03.110
We were so lucky to have him for four seasons.
我们很幸运能拥有他四个季度。

87
00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:09.070
And Office Ladies has been so lucky that he saved like everything.
而且《办公室女士》也非常幸运，因为他几乎保存了一切。

88
00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.250
Talk about digital hoarder.
说起数字囤积狂。

89
00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:14.310
Kentopedia is giving you a run for your money, Angela.
“肯特百科”快要赶上你了，安吉拉。

90
00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:15.970
Well, I think he's beat me.
嗯，我觉得他已经超过我了。

91
00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:17.250
But I just love him.
但我就是很喜欢他。

92
00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.070
And we loved him so much.
我们也非常爱他。

93
00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:25.930
Jenna, in anticipation of this being his last episode, I went through and found all of these
珍娜，为了迎接这是他最后一集的到来，我翻找并整理了

94
00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:28.970
emails during this week that I traded with Kent.
这一周里我和肯特往来的所有邮件。

95
00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:31.250
This was like towards the end of my pregnancy.
那时正值我怀孕后期。

96
00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:37.290
And he and I were having to schedule a lot of things around my OBGYN appointments and everything.
我和他当时不得不围绕我的产科医生预约等事宜安排很多工作。

97
00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:42.930
And if I could share anything with you guys is the kindness and the thoughtfulness that this
如果说有什么我想和大家分享的，那就是这个男人

98
00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:47.990
man had for every member of the cast and making the show the best it could be.
对每一位演员所展现出的善良和体贴，以及他为让这部剧达到最佳效果所做的努力。

99
00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.410
And we were so sad to see him go.
我们非常难过看到他离开。

100
00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:53.030
I just love this guy.
我真的太喜欢这家伙了。

101
00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.250
I love him, too.
我也很爱他。

102
00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:56.250
And I love being in touch with him.
而且我很喜欢和他保持联系。

103
00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:57.990
And he was so great to us on The Office.
他在《办公室》剧组时对我们特别好。

104
00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.030
And he's been so great to us on Office Ladies.
他在《办公室女士》节目里也一直对我们很好。

105
00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:01.470
We love you, Kentopedia.
我们爱你，肯特百科全书。

106
00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:03.410
We love you, Kentopedia.
我们爱你，肯特百科全书。

107
00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:07.070
And I'm going to share a few of our emails later in this episode.
稍后我会在本集节目中分享几封我们的邮件。

108
00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:13.250
Angela, I want to share one of my favorite fun facts about Kent as we say goodbye to him.
安吉拉，在和肯特告别之际，我想分享一个关于他我最喜欢的趣事。

109
00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:14.170
Okay, what?
好啊，是什么？

110
00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:20.670
In his youth, Kent was an assistant to the creator of Golden Girls.
年轻时，肯特曾是《黄金女郎》主创的助理。

111
00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:27.630
Her name is Susan Harris, and she loved Kent's last name so much that when she wrote Golden
她叫苏珊·哈里斯，她非常喜欢肯特的姓氏，所以在写《黄金女郎》时，

112
00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:32.550
Girls, she named Bea Arthur's character Dorothy Zabornak.
她把碧·亚瑟饰演的角色命名为多萝西·扎博纳克。

113
00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:34.110
Amazing!
太神奇了！

114
00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:35.170
Yes!
没错！

115
00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.770
He was the inspiration behind that name.
他就是那个名字背后的灵感来源。

116
00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:41.530
He told me he was beyond excited by this honor.
他告诉我，他因为这份殊荣感到无比激动。

117
00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:43.430
He was like, I mean, who wouldn't be?
他说，我的意思是，谁会不激动呢？

118
00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:47.790
And then he went on to be the first assistant director on Golden Girls.
后来他还担任了《黄金女郎》的第一助理导演。

119
00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:51.050
And he said Bea Arthur was like a second mother to him.
他说碧·亚瑟对他来说就像第二个母亲一样。

120
00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.150
He just loved her.
他真的很爱她。

121
00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:54.410
That is so wonderful.
那真是太美好了。

122
00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:55.770
I love all of that.
我喜欢这一切。

123
00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:56.910
We love you, Kent.
我们爱你，肯特。

124
00:05:57.910 --> 00:05:59.930
Okay, rounding out my fast facts.
好了，来总结一下我的快讯。

125
00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:01.330
Fast fact number three.
快讯第三条。

126
00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:04.630
Angela, you came up with this idea, and I just loved it.
安吉拉，这个主意是你提出来的，我特别喜欢。

127
00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:08.210
I think we should do it for every character.
我觉得我们应该为每个角色都做一次。

128
00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:10.250
And now I'm like, oh, we might have missed a few.
现在我在想，哦，我们可能漏掉了一些。

129
00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:14.550
We might have to, in a revisited, do this for other characters.
我们可能得在重温节目时，为其他角色也补上。

130
00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:15.630
That's right.
没错。

131
00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.270
Here's what we're talking about.
我们要说的就是这个。

132
00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:22.670
Angela said, whenever we say goodbye to a character, we should give them a show Bible
安吉拉说，每当我们和某个角色告别时，都应该根据剧集设定集

133
00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:23.030
goodbye.
来和他们告别。

134
00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:29.130
So I went through the show Bible, and I gathered facts about Toby Flunderson.
所以我翻阅了剧集设定集，收集了关于托比·弗兰德森的事实。

135
00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:29.770
Yay!
耶！

136
00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:31.750
Here they are.
都在这儿了。

137
00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:37.430
Toby Flunderson, graduate of Bishop O'Hara High School, class of 89.
托比·弗兰德森，主教奥哈拉高中89届毕业生。

138
00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:44.510
He is divorced, but his wife is still his emergency contact, although her last name is Becker now.
他离异了，但他的前妻仍是他的紧急联系人，尽管她现在改姓贝克了。

139
00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:45.550
Hmm.
嗯。

140
00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:52.790
During his 12 years working HR at Dunder Mifflin, he has explained female anatomy to Dwight, told
在他担任邓德·米夫林人力资源部经理的12年里，他曾向德怀特解释过女性生理结构，

141
00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:57.530
Kevin he should ditch Dunder Mifflin's health care plan and get on his fiancee Stacy's plan
告诉凯文他应该放弃邓德·米夫林的医保计划，转而加入他未婚妻史黛西的计划，

142
00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:59.730
instead because it's definitely going to be better.
因为那肯定会更好。

143
00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:06.450
He sent out a memo regarding Jim and Pam's PDA, and he attended Jan's deposition and was
他发过关于吉姆和帕姆公开秀恩爱的备忘录，参加过简的取证会，

144
00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:08.350
present for the reading of Michael's diary.
还在场见证了迈克尔日记的宣读。

145
00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:11.710
Toby is one of the founding members of the Finer Things Club.
托比是“精致事物俱乐部”的创始成员之一。

146
00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:17.290
He bought Angela her baby jazz poster, and he can run a mile in seven minutes.
他给安吉拉买了那张爵士乐宝宝海报，而且他七分钟能跑完一英里。

147
00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:22.550
He's been trying to flirt with Pam and ask her out ever since season three.
从第三季开始，他就一直试图和帕姆调情并约她出去。

148
00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:26.290
That is also how long he's been talking about going to Costa Rica.
这也是他念叨要去哥斯达黎加念叨了多久的时间。

149
00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:30.690
He started talking about that ever since he heard the Scranton branch might be closing.
他从听说斯克兰顿分公司可能要关闭时就开始说这件事了。

150
00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:36.250
And now, after a very awkward moment of rubbing Pam's knee, he is finally leaving.
现在，在经历了抚摸帕姆膝盖的尴尬时刻后，他终于要离开了。

151
